1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,880
Does ruqyah replace the doctor?

2
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:04,080
Many people get the answer wrong.

3
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:06,330
The Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

4
00:00:06,570 --> 00:00:07,960
“Allah has not sent down a disease

5
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,590
except that He sent down a cure for it.”

6
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,970
(As in Sahih al-Bukhari)

7
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:11,810
And he said:

8
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,220
“Seek treatment, servants of Allah.”

9
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:17,130
The Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ruqyah and had ruqyah performed for him,

10
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,220
and at the same time

11
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:20,050
he sought treatment and commanded treatment,

12
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:21,860
so the two never conflicted for him.

13
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,020
Ruqyah is supplication and reliance on Allah,

14
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:27,230
and the doctor is one of the means of healing,

15
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,410
and both are by Allah’s permission alone.

16
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,770
So do not abandon the doctor on the pretext of ruqyah,

17
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,150
and do not abandon ruqyah on the pretext of the doctor.

18
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:37,660
Combine the two, as the Prophet (peace be upon him) did.

19
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:41,560
Send this clip to someone you love, and follow the channel.

